# Security Guidelines

## Sensitive Data

- NEVER hardcode secrets, API keys, or passwords
- NEVER commit .env files or credentials
- Use environment variables for all sensitive config
- Mask sensitive data in logs (use `[REDACTED]`)

## Authentication

- All API routes require auth middleware (except public endpoints)
- Use JWT tokens with appropriate expiration
- Validate tokens on every request
- Hash passwords with bcrypt (never store plaintext)

## Database Security

- ALWAYS use parameterized queries
- NEVER concatenate user input into SQL strings
- Validate and sanitize all user inputs
- Use the validation middleware for request bodies

## API Security

- Validate request bodies before processing
- Return generic error messages to clients (no stack traces)
- Log detailed errors server-side only
- Use HTTPS in production

## File Handling

- Validate file types and sizes before upload
- Never execute user-uploaded files
- Store uploads outside web root

## Code Review Checklist

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] Input validation present
- [ ] Parameterized queries used
- [ ] Auth middleware applied
- [ ] Error messages don't leak internals
